<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balowoka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balowoka, &quot;those who crossed&quot;, is the name given in Tumbuka tradition to traders and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> hunters who crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malawi">Lake Malawi</a> from the east in the late 18th century. Their leader, remembered as Gonapamuhanya, settled in the north of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a>, and his descendants founded the Chikulamayembe dynasty, which held loose authority over Tumbuka clans until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngoni">Ngoni</a> invasions of the mid-19th century.</p></div>
